                  <provenance type="#s"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_601">Worcester, Worcestershire.
                     Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>Catalogue of s.
                     xvii in no. 221: <q>Ex synodis excerpta ... Initium Synodorum exemplarium
                     innumerositatem ... Canones Adomani Initium Marina animalia ... vetus fol. bon.
                     </q></p><p>At Worcester in s. xi as appears from the hand of corrections near
                     the end; this hand occurs in other Worcester MSS.</p><note
                     type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Young 221</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_224">Glastonbury,
                     Somerset, Benedictine Abbey of Saint Mary the Virgin</orgName> <p>This
                     attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                     corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records the
                     following information, which was deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution:
                     <q>Liber sancti Dunstani</q>.</p> <p>Compare the catalogue entry in
                     <title>Medieval Manuscripts in Oxford Libraries</title> (linked below): <q>A
                     Glastonbury provenance was suggested in the <title>Summary Catalogue</title>,
                     based mainly on an inscription on the former spine (now preserved on the lower
                     pastedown) read as <q>Liber Sc Dunsani</q> and understood as referring to St
                     Dunstan. Bruce Barker-Benfield (<ref
                     target="https://doi.org/10.1093/nq/40-4-431"
                     >https://doi.org/10.1093/nq/40-4-431</ref>) argued that the correct reading was
                     ‘Liber S' Ƿufsani’, identified as Wulfstan II of Worcester (d.
                     1095).</q></p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Used by <persName>Matthew Parker</persName>
                     and <persName>John Joscelyn</persName>.</provenance>
               </history>
